# Hexplain Aspect — Raster (hx-raster) 1.3
# Content-representation aspect: a regular N-D grid of samples. Sibling of hx-geometry
# (vector); neither imports the other. Imports no other aspect.
@prefix :        <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#> .
@prefix araster: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix ma:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/ma-ont#> .
@prefix asamp:   <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/sampling#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vann:    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster/1.3> ; owl:versionInfo "1.3" ;
    <http://schema.org/creativeWorkStatus> "working draft" ;
    owl:priorVersion <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster/1.2> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-09-27"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "Hexplain Aspect — Raster (hx-raster)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Content-representation aspect for a regular N-dimensional sample grid (width, height). Colour (hx-color) and per-sample precision (hx-sampling) compose with it at the vocabulary that describes the medium; neither is imported. Shared by image, video frames, and geospatial rasters."@en ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-22"^^xsd:date ; dcterms:creator <https://geoknoesis.com> ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "araster" ; vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#" .

:width a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "width"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:seeAlso ma:frameWidth ; rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ; rdfs:comment "Grid extent along the horizontal axis, in samples (pixels)."@en .
:height a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "height"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:seeAlso ma:frameHeight ; rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ; rdfs:comment "Grid extent along the vertical axis, in samples (pixels)."@en .
:noDataValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "no-data value"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Sample value denoting absence of data, on a band or on the grid (inherited by bands that state none). A numeric literal: xsd:double or xsd:float (including NaN, which matches NaN samples), xsd:decimal, or an integer-family datatype. At most one per band or grid. No rdfs:range is asserted because the admissible datatypes are a union; RasterBandShape enforces it."@en .

# 1.1 working draft: logical samples, independent of physical storage layout.
:RasterGrid a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Raster grid"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "A two-dimensional grid with one or more co-registered bands. Higher-dimensional arrays use SampleArray; physical byte addressing remains in DLV."@en .
:RasterBand a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Raster band"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "One sample plane of a raster grid, with its own sample interpretation, no-data, calibration and optional mask."@en .
:SampleArray a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Sample array"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "A logical array of arbitrary rank, including rank-zero scalars and zero-length dimensions. Logical dimension order is independent of physical byte strides and chunk order."@en .
:ArrayDimension a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Array dimension"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "A reusable named axis with an extent. Its position belongs to each array's ordered dimension list, not to the shared dimension."@en .
:ArrayGroup a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Array group"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "A logical hierarchy of groups and arrays. It does not imply filesystem directory layout."@en .
:hasBand a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :RasterBand ; rdfs:label "has band"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> .
:bandCount a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ; rdfs:label "band count"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Total band count. A partial RDF projection may describe fewer bands, but never more than this count."@en .
:bandIndex a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ; rdfs:label "band index"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "One-based band index within its owning grid."@en .
:sampleScale a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:double ; rdfs:label "sample scale"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Calibration multiplier: physical = raw * sampleScale + sampleOffset. Absence means unspecified, not a stored default. Apply no-data detection to raw samples first."@en .
:sampleOffset a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:double ; rdfs:label "sample offset"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Calibration additive term, in the unit of the physical value. Independent of byte offsets and georeferencing origins."@en .
:sampleUnit a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "sample unit"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Unit IRI for calibrated sample values; profiles may reuse established unit vocabularies."@en .
:hasMask a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :RasterBand ; rdfs:label "has validity mask"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Validity mask band: zero is invalid; nonzero is valid. This relation does not imply alpha/transparency semantics."@en .
:hasOverview a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "has overview"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "A lower-resolution representation covering the same logical domain. Does not assert a resampling algorithm or an integer reduction factor."@en .
:dimensions a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range rdf:List ; rdfs:label "dimensions"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Complete ordered RDF list of ArrayDimension resources in logical indexing order. rdf:nil denotes a scalar. The list must be finite, well formed and permit repeated dimension resources at distinct positions."@en .
:dimensionName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:label "dimension name"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> .
:dimensionExtent a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; rdfs:label "dimension extent"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Current number of indexable values along this logical axis. Zero is permitted. An unlimited dimension has a finite current extent, not infinity."@en .
:dimensionKind a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range skos:Concept ; rdfs:label "dimension kind"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Axis nature from a profile-bound concept scheme; no fixed list limits scientific or non-spatial axes."@en .
:coordinateArray a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :SampleArray ; rdfs:label "coordinate array"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ; rdfs:comment "Array of coordinate values associated with a dimension. Its shape and alignment are asserted by the profile; coordinates need not be regularly spaced."@en .
:hasArray a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :SampleArray ; rdfs:label "has array"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> .
:hasGroup a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :ArrayGroup ; rdfs:label "has group"@en ; rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> .

# RDF datatypes retain the wire value's precision; SHACL accepts the integer family.
# Kept local rather than referencing asamp:PositiveIntegerShape: shapes are validated module by
# module (the family contracts and the engine load one module's shapes), and a sh:node into another
# module's graph would silently accept every value when that module is not loaded.
:PositiveCountShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:positiveInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:int ] [ sh:datatype xsd:long ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedInt ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedLong ] [ sh:datatype xsd:short ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedShort ] [ sh:datatype xsd:byte ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedByte ] ) ; sh:minExclusive 0 .
:ExtentShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:positiveInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:int ] [ sh:datatype xsd:long ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedInt ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedLong ] ) ; sh:minInclusive 0 .
:RasterSizeShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :width, :height, :bandCount ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :width ; sh:node :PositiveCountShape ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :height ; sh:node :PositiveCountShape ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :bandCount ; sh:node :PositiveCountShape ; sh:maxCount 1 ] .
:RasterBandShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetClass :RasterBand ; sh:targetObjectsOf :hasBand, :hasMask ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :sampleScale, :sampleOffset, :bandIndex, :noDataValue, :sampleUnit ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:property [ sh:path [ sh:inversePath :hasBand ] ; sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A band belongs to at most one grid (araster:hasBand): no-data inheritance and band indexing need a single owning grid." ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :bandIndex ; sh:node :PositiveCountShape ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :sampleScale ; sh:datatype xsd:double ; sh:maxCount 1 ; sh:minExclusive "-INF"^^xsd:double ; sh:maxExclusive "INF"^^xsd:double ; sh:not [ sh:pattern "^(nan|[+-]?inf)$" ; sh:flags "i" ] ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :sampleOffset ; sh:datatype xsd:double ; sh:maxCount 1 ; sh:minExclusive "-INF"^^xsd:double ; sh:maxExclusive "INF"^^xsd:double ; sh:not [ sh:pattern "^(nan|[+-]?inf)$" ; sh:flags "i" ] ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :noDataValue ; sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:positiveInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:nonPositiveInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:negativeInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:long ] [ sh:datatype xsd:int ] [ sh:datatype xsd:short ] [ sh:datatype xsd:byte ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedLong ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedInt ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedShort ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedByte ] ) ;
        sh:message "araster:noDataValue is at most one numeric literal (xsd:double/float, including NaN; xsd:decimal; or an integer-family datatype)." ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :sampleUnit ; sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ; sh:maxCount 1 ] .
:BandMembershipShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :hasBand ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :hasBand ; sh:node :RasterBandShape ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:message "Band indexes must be unique within one grid and may not exceed its declared count." ; sh:select """
      PREFIX a: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#>
      SELECT $this WHERE {
        { $this a:hasBand ?b, ?c . ?b a:bandIndex ?i . ?c a:bandIndex ?j . FILTER(!sameTerm(?b, ?c) && ?i = ?j) }
        UNION { $this a:hasBand ?b ; a:bandCount ?n . ?b a:bandIndex ?i . FILTER(?i > ?n) }
      }
    """ ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:message "Described bands exceed the declared total." ; sh:select """
      PREFIX a: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#>
      SELECT $this WHERE { $this a:bandCount ?n . { SELECT $this (COUNT(DISTINCT ?b) AS ?c) WHERE { $this a:hasBand ?b } GROUP BY $this } FILTER(?c > ?n) }
    """ ] .
:ArrayDimensionShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetClass :ArrayDimension ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :dimensionExtent ; sh:node :ExtentShape ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :dimensionName ; sh:datatype xsd:string ; sh:minLength 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :dimensionKind ; sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :coordinateArray ; sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ; sh:maxCount 1 ] .
:SampleArrayShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetClass :SampleArray ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :dimensions ; sh:targetObjectsOf :hasArray, :coordinateArray ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :dimensions ; sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path ( :dimensions [ sh:zeroOrMorePath rdf:rest ] rdf:first ) ; sh:node :ArrayDimensionShape ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:message "Dimension lists must terminate in rdf:nil, contain exactly one first/rest per cell, and contain no cycles." ; sh:select """
      PREFIX a: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#>
      PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
      SELECT DISTINCT $this WHERE {
        $this a:dimensions ?head .
        { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?head rdf:rest* rdf:nil } }
        UNION { ?head rdf:rest* ?cell . FILTER(?cell != rdf:nil) FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?cell rdf:first ?v ; rdf:rest ?r } }
        UNION { ?head rdf:rest* ?cell . ?cell rdf:first ?v, ?w . FILTER(!sameTerm(?v, ?w)) }
        UNION { ?head rdf:rest* ?cell . ?cell rdf:rest ?v, ?w . FILTER(!sameTerm(?v, ?w)) }
        UNION { ?head rdf:rest* ?cell . ?cell rdf:rest+ ?cell }
        UNION { ?head rdf:rest* rdf:nil . rdf:nil ?p ?v . FILTER(?p IN (rdf:first,rdf:rest)) }
      }
    """ ] .
:GroupHierarchyShape a sh:NodeShape ; sh:targetSubjectsOf :hasGroup ;
    sh:property [ sh:path :hasGroup ; sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:message "Group containment must be acyclic." ; sh:select """
      PREFIX a: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#>
      SELECT $this WHERE { $this a:hasGroup+ $this }
    """ ] .

# ---------- Range datatype shapes ----------
# Each XSD rdfs:range above, enforced wherever the property is used: activation is by
# subjects-of, so an untyped subject is checked too (tools/test_range_datatypes.py).
# Integer ranges accept any XSD integer-family datatype within the range's bounds.
araster:RangeDatatypeShape a sh:NodeShape ; rdfs:label "Range datatype shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf araster:dimensionExtent ,
        araster:dimensionName ;
    sh:property [ sh:path araster:dimensionExtent ; sh:node :ExtentShape ;
        sh:message "araster:dimensionExtent takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger)." ] ;
    sh:property [ sh:path araster:dimensionName ; sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:message "araster:dimensionName takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string)." ] .

# BEGIN GENERATED TERM DOCUMENTATION
# Editorial annotations only; OWL axioms and SHACL constraints above are unchanged.
@prefix araster: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> skos:scopeNote "Use for logical raster samples, bands and arrays after parsing. Logical dimensions are independent of physical DLV addressing; partial graphs and complete dimension lists have different completeness contracts."@en .
araster:ArrayDimensionShape rdfs:label "Array Dimension Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of araster:ArrayDimension. Each focus node is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). araster:coordinateArray takes at most one value; each is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). araster:dimensionExtent takes exactly one value, a value conforming to araster:ExtentShape. araster:dimensionKind takes at most one value; each is an IRI. araster:dimensionName takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal at least 1 character long."@en .
araster:BandMembershipShape rdfs:label "Band Membership Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using araster:hasBand. Each value of araster:hasBand is a value conforming to araster:RasterBandShape. Band indexes must be unique within one grid and may not exceed its declared count. Described bands exceed the declared total."@en .
araster:ExtentShape rdfs:label "Extent Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) at least 0."@en .
araster:GroupHierarchyShape rdfs:label "Group Hierarchy Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using araster:hasGroup. Each value of araster:hasGroup is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). Group containment must be acyclic."@en .
araster:PositiveCountShape rdfs:label "Positive Count Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0."@en .
araster:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using araster:dimensionExtent, araster:dimensionName. araster:dimensionExtent takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). araster:dimensionName takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string)."@en .
araster:RasterBandShape rdfs:label "Raster Band Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of araster:RasterBand; subjects using araster:bandIndex, araster:noDataValue, araster:sampleOffset, araster:sampleScale, araster:sampleUnit; objects of araster:hasBand, araster:hasMask. Each focus node is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). araster:bandIndex takes at most one value; each is a value conforming to araster:PositiveCountShape. araster:noDataValue is at most one numeric literal (xsd:double/float, including NaN; xsd:decimal; or an integer-family datatype). araster:sampleOffset takes at most one value; each is an xsd:double literal greater than -inf, less than inf, not a value matching the regular expression ^(nan|[+-]?inf)$ (flags \"i\"). araster:sampleScale takes at most one value; each is an xsd:double literal greater than -inf, less than inf, not a value matching the regular expression ^(nan|[+-]?inf)$ (flags \"i\"). araster:sampleUnit takes at most one value; each is an IRI. A band belongs to at most one grid (araster:hasBand): no-data inheritance and band indexing need a single owning grid."@en .
araster:RasterSizeShape rdfs:label "Raster Size Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using araster:bandCount, araster:height, araster:width. araster:bandCount takes at most one value; each is a value conforming to araster:PositiveCountShape. araster:height takes at most one value; each is a value conforming to araster:PositiveCountShape. araster:width takes at most one value; each is a value conforming to araster:PositiveCountShape."@en .
araster:SampleArrayShape rdfs:label "Sample Array Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of araster:SampleArray; subjects using araster:dimensions; objects of araster:coordinateArray, araster:hasArray. araster:dimensions takes exactly one value, a resource (an IRI or a blank node). Each member of the araster:dimensions list is a value conforming to araster:ArrayDimensionShape. Dimension lists must terminate in rdf:nil, contain exactly one first/rest per cell, and contain no cycles."@en .
araster:dimensionName skos:definition "The source-level name of a logical array dimension, independent of its position in any one array."@en .
araster:hasArray skos:definition "A logical array contained in a group, independent of its physical storage path."@en .
araster:hasBand skos:definition "A band view belonging to a raster grid. A reused physical sample plane may need distinct band views when its position differs between grids."@en .
araster:hasGroup skos:definition "A logical child group within an acyclic array-group hierarchy."@en .
